SHIP mesh-seat 0c7ec63d3a9f0fb81cf053c7991bbe5d5b69961d
read: the span's held-out lane (the land train's DIRECT-over-red rule): its own held-out run 42398135251 at 0c7ec63d3a9f0fb81cf053c7991bbe5d5b69961d reads GREEN on every cell (the mesh scenarios, herm-mesh, herm-mesh-roll, browser-weld W3) and CI 42398135346 GREEN; reserve-seat collide (Lares-Kiaʻi, Opus) of 841065fcd: pono (the PACING reason, the one-shot MessageChannel yield, the flight queue) with one gap (a read mid-pause), answered at 0c7ec63d3a9f0fb81cf053c7991bbe5d5b69961d by construction plus a pinned test whose negative control fails without the flight queue; controller read each step's handback and the container-founding audit (only the mesh compose and test tools reach lararium-container-boot.sh; production composes and the Dockerfile stay unseated); Kiaʻi's three guards hold (test composes only, one seat, held-out on the cure's head).
owed: the browser return leg's remaining silent refusals in vessel-host.ts:450 (session-unadmitted, light failure; pending stays silent), before the rite; the plugin byte move declared in genesis/unbaked.json for the pre-rite re-bake; "one founding harness, named once" as a row after the rite.

